{"chunk_id": "002e122ba025", "text": "The sage Javali argues to Rama that obligations to the dead and to scriptural duty are illusions. Using bluntly materialist reasoning, he urges Rama to abandon exile and accept the throne from Bharata, claiming there is no afterlife and that rituals and scriptures are inventions meant to extract wealth from the naive. Rama firmly rejects this counsel. Speaking from Vedic principles, he insists that truth, duty, and fidelity to one\u2019s word sustain both kingdom and cosmos. A ruler\u2019s conduct shapes the people, and breaking his vow would destroy moral order. Rama declares that honoring his father\u2019s promise and upholding truth outweigh the lure of kingship, condemning atheistic doctrines as dangerous to society.\nRama rebuts Javali\u2019s materialist advice, defending Vedic authority, truth, and his duty to honor his father\u2019s vow and remain in exile.\nThemes: truth as supreme virtue, Vedic authority, duty to father, kingship and moral example, rejection of materialism", "vector": [0.009120951406657696, -0.016102829948067665, -0.014096619561314583, 5.900924952584319e-05, -0.004504009149968624, 0.012063836678862572, -0.03536776825785637, -0.020075391978025436, -0.03005330078303814, 0.00012798311945516616, 0.010270204395055771, 0.013053655624389648, 0.017657311633229256, 0.01596996746957302, -0.018427908420562744, -0.008131131529808044, 0.06329528242349625, -0.021138286218047142, 0.031355343759059906, -0.001785328146070242, 0.004477437119930983, -0.010569143109023571, -0.010323348455131054, -0.01007091160863638, -0.008157704025506973, 0.0068490169942379, 0.022280896082520485, -0.02038097381591797, 0.014973506331443787, -0.022785769775509834, -0.002497798763215542, -0.01927822269499302, 2.91121386908344e-06, -0.014933647587895393, -0.024698978289961815, 0.015039936639368534, -0.01618254743516445, -0.008795440196990967, 0.0018534198170527816, 0.003643730189651251, 0.013631603680551052, -0.004055601544678211, -0.01032334